@*
    ── Lecturer Home (Dashboard) ────────────────────────────────────────────
    Visual source: the FINISHED Motiva dashboards that are live in this repo —
                   MentorHomePage (בית) and the student Dashboard, which was
                   itself aligned to the mentor's grammar. Those two screens,
                   not the older MotivaLecturerDesign exports, are the source
                   of truth for every value on this page.
    Data source:   IDashboardOverviewService.GetAsync("lecturer")
                   → DashboardOverviewDto — UNCHANGED. Every count, every
                   shortlist, every derivation below is the one that was here
                   before this pass.

    ── WHAT THIS PASS CHANGED, AND WHAT IT DID NOT ──────────────────────────
    Presentation only. The lecturer's information architecture is intact:
    greeting + portfolio sentence, four portfolio counters, "דורש את תשומת
    לבך" over the same three sources in the same priority and the same caps,
    "צוותים שדורשים תשומת לב", "בקרוב", and the attention popup with its own
    detail rows and CTA. No query, no cap, no ordering and no permission
    moved.

    What it adopted from the finished screens:
      • the card grammar — solid #FFFFFF at radius-xl, one lifted card
        wearing the three-hue glow and the rest on a violet-tinted hairline
      • section heads — a bare 16px violet glyph, no container chip
      • row grammar — an rgba(27,26,34,.06) floor, none on the last, and ink
        that moves to violet on hover with no wash behind it
      • the four semantic tones (alert · request · wait · ok) as CLASSES, so
        the page no longer carries a single inline hex
      • בקרוב's 46px date tile, day over month
      • the density scale and its viewport bands, so the default dashboard
        answers itself in one look on a laptop

    TWO CORRECTIONS OF FACT, both inside this page:
      • Summary.SubmissionsMissing counts required submissions that are PAST
        DUE WITH NOTHING ATTACHED (LecturerDashboardController, query 2b).
        The pill called them "הגשות לאישורך" — submissions awaiting your
        approval — while BuildDesc, two blocks down, called the same number
        "הגשות חסרות". One number, two contradictory names, on one screen.
        It is "הגשות חסרות" everywhere now, which is what the query counts.
      • the same item's CTA pointed at /assignments — the Admin-only שיבוצים
        (team-matching) page. A Staff lecturer following it was refused
        outright, and an Admin landed somewhere with nothing to do with
        submissions. It points at /lecturer/submissions, the הגשות ובקרה
        destination this role's own nav carries.

    ── LAYOUT ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        greeting + portfolio sentence
        four counter pills
        ┌ דורש את תשומת לבך      1.75fr ─┬ בקרוב              1fr ─┐
        └─────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────┘
        ┌ צוותים שדורשים תשומת לב — full width ────────────────────┐
        └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

    The second row is FULL WIDTH rather than the mentor's checkerboard,
    because this is the one place the two roles genuinely differ: a mentor
    reads four supervised teams and a lecturer reads a portfolio. The row
    keeps its three facts on ONE line each — team · מנחה · why it is here —
    which is both the shape it already had and the shape that lets a
    five-team list cost 42px a row instead of 64. That is what pays for the
    six-deep attention card above it fitting on a laptop.
*@
@page "/dashboard/lecturer"
@layout AppLayout
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = Roles.Admin + "," + Roles.Staff + "," + Roles.Mentor)]
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Components
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Services
@using AuthWithAdmin.Shared.AuthSharedModels
@inject IDashboardOverviewService DashboardService

@* ── The section glyphs' ink ──
   ONE <linearGradient>, referenced by all three section marks — the same
   device המשימות שלי uses, and for the same reason: an SVG stroke resolves a
   paint server, not a CSS background, so the gradient has to be a document
   node. Defining it once keeps the three marks provably identical.

   Rendered outside the loading branch so the reference is never dangling. *@
<svg class="ldh-grad-def" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    <defs>
        <linearGradient id="ldhIconGradient" x1="1" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
            <stop offset="0%"   stop-color="#6D28F5" />
            <stop offset="60%"  stop-color="#2E63E8" />
            <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#0FA8C2" />
        </linearGradient>
    </defs>
</svg>

<div class="ldh-page">

    @* ── Title + the portfolio reading ──────────────────────────────────
       MPageHeader Compact, which is המשימות שלי's own header — so the
       greeting, its ambient band and its inline measure are not this page's
       decisions any more, they are the component's.

       THE FOUR PORTFOLIO NUMBERS MOVED INTO THE ACTIONS SLOT. They were a
       strip of four white pills on a row of their own: four surfaces, four
       category-coloured dots, and 32px of page height spent restating what
       the cards below already show. In the slot המשימות שלי fills with its
       filter tabs, they cost no band at all and read as what they are — a
       masthead reading opposite the greeting, not four widgets.

       They are still plain spans. A mentor's shortcut pills are links
       because each opens the queue that owns its number; "7 צוותים פעילים"
       has no single destination, so it stays text. *@
    <MPageHeader Variant="MPageHeader.HeaderVariant.Compact" Title="@_greeting">
        <Actions>
            @if (!_loading && !_loadError && _data is not null)
            {
                <div class="ldh-stats" aria-label="סיכום התיק">
                    <span class="ldh-stat">
                        <span class="ldh-stat-num">@_data.Summary.TotalProjects</span>
                        <span class="ldh-stat-label">צוותים פעילים</span>
                    </span>
                    <span class="ldh-stat">
                        <span class="ldh-stat-num">@_data.Summary.OpenRequests</span>
                        <span class="ldh-stat-label">בקשות להחלטתך</span>
                    </span>
                    <span class="ldh-stat">
                        <span class="ldh-stat-num">@_data.Summary.SubmissionsMissing</span>
                        <span class="ldh-stat-label">הגשות חסרות</span>
                    </span>
                    @* The one reading that names a problem, so the one that
                       carries rose — and only while there is something to
                       carry it about. At zero it is an ordinary number. *@
                    <span class="ldh-stat @(_data.Summary.OverdueTasks > 0 ? "ldh-stat-late" : "")">
                        <span class="ldh-stat-num">@_data.Summary.OverdueTasks</span>
                        <span class="ldh-stat-label">משימות באיחור</span>
                    </span>
                </div>
            }
        </Actions>
    </MPageHeader>

    @if (_loading)
    {
        <MLoadingState Label="טוענת נתונים…" />
    }
    else if (_loadError || _data is null)
    {
        <p class="ldh-error">שגיאה בטעינת הדשבורד. נסה לרענן את הדף.</p>
    }
    else
    {
        @* ── ROW 1 — דורש את תשומת לבך (1.75fr) · בקרוב (1fr) ─────────── *@
        <div class="ldh-row ldh-row-1">

            @* ── 1. דורש את תשומת לבך ───────────────────────────────
                 One MCard, one MSectionHeading, one MRowList — the same
                 three components המשימות שלי builds every panel from, so
                 the surface, the radius, the heading and the row are not
                 restated here at all.

                 THE LEADING BAR IS GONE. Every row carried a 4x40 gradient
                 column at the reading start; the reference sheet records
                 "avoid large colored vertical bars on every row" as a
                 standing instruction, and six of them down one card was the
                 loudest thing on the dashboard. State reaches the eye
                 through the row's own chip now, which is where המשימות שלי
                 puts it.

                 The chevron went with it: MRow renders a real <button>, and
                 an arrow on every line of a six-deep list is chrome
                 repeating what the cursor already says. *@
            <div class="ldh-col">
                <section class="ldh-pane" aria-labelledby="ldh-attn-h">
                    <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None" Fill="true">
                        <div class="ldh-card ldh-card-attn">
                            <div class="ldh-card-head">
                                <MSectionHeading Class="ldh-head" Text="דורש את תשומת לבך"
                                                 Count="@CountLabel(AttentionItems.Count)"
                                                 LabelId="ldh-attn-h">
                                    <Icon>
                                        <span class="ldh-ico">
                                            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="url(#ldhIconGradient)"
                                                 stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                                <path d="M18 8.4a6 6 0 1 0-12 0c0 5.9-2.2 7.4-2.2 7.4h16.4S18 14.3 18 8.4"></path>
                                                <path d="M13.7 19.7a2 2 0 0 1-3.4 0"></path>
                                            </svg>
                                        </span>
                                    </Icon>
                                </MSectionHeading>
                            </div>

                            @if (AttentionItems.Count == 0)
                            {
                                <MEmptyState Title="הכול תחת שליטה."
                                             Description="אין בקשות, הגשות או פרויקטים שדורשים את התייחסותך כרגע."
                                             Class="ldh-empty" />
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <MRowList AriaLabel="פריטים הדורשים את תשומת לבך">
                                    @foreach (var item in AttentionItems)
                                    {
                                        var it = item;
                                        <MRow OnClick="@(() => OpenPopup(it))"
                                              Primary="@it.Title"
                                              Secondary="@it.Fact"
                                              Status="@TagChip(it.Tag, it.Tone)"
                                              Meta="@it.Due"
                                              MetaTone="@DueMetaTone(it.DueClass)"
                                              AriaLabel="@($"{it.Title} — {it.Fact}, {it.Tag}. הצגת פרטים")" />
                                    }
                                </MRowList>
                            }
                        </div>
                    </MCard>
                </section>
            </div>

            @* ── 2. לוח זמנים ───────────────────────────────────────
                 NAMED FOR WHAT IT IS. "בקרוב" described a moment ("soon"),
                 which is a claim about urgency — and half this list is
                 already past, so the title was arguing with its own rows.
                 "לוח זמנים" names the OBJECT instead: where the teams'
                 milestones fall in time. It also keeps a clean distance from
                 the product's next-task concept (ProjectContextDto's
                 NextTaskTitle / NextTaskDueDate, which the student focus
                 card renders) — that answers what to DO next, where this
                 answers when things are DUE. The obvious middle option,
                 "הבא בתור", would have read as exactly that concept
                 arriving on the lecturer's screen. Same query, same order,
                 same five rows.

                 THE RELATIVE TIMING IS A CHIP, not floating rose text. As
                 bare ink at semibold it read as an alarm printed on the row
                 — and with this cohort every row is past, so the card was a
                 column of red sentences. In the product's own chip language
                 it is an annotation ON the row instead: rose only where the
                 milestone has genuinely passed, the restrained brand tint
                 where one is close, neutral where it is simply scheduled.
                 The milestone title stays the primary fact. *@
            <section class="ldh-pane" aria-labelledby="ldh-up-h">
                <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None" Fill="true">
                    <div class="ldh-card ldh-card-cal">
                        <div class="ldh-card-head">
                            <MSectionHeading Class="ldh-head" Text="לוח זמנים"
                                             LinkHref="/milestones-overview" LinkText="ליומן המלא"
                                             LabelId="ldh-up-h">
                                <Icon>
                                    <span class="ldh-ico">
                                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="url(#ldhIconGradient)"
                                             stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                            <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="18" rx="3"></rect>
                                            <path d="M16 2v4M8 2v4M3 10h18"></path>
                                        </svg>
                                    </span>
                                </Icon>
                            </MSectionHeading>
                        </div>

                        @if (!UpcomingItems.Any())
                        {
                            <MEmptyState Title="אין אבני דרך בלוח הזמנים."
                                         Description="אבני הדרך של הצוותים יופיעו כאן."
                                         Class="ldh-empty" />
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <MRowList AriaLabel="לוח הזמנים של אבני הדרך">
                                @foreach (var u in UpcomingItems)
                                {
                                    <MRow Primary="@u.Title"
                                          Secondary="@UpcomingContext(u)"
                                          Status="@WhenChip(u.When, u.WhenClass)"
                                          AriaLabel="@($"{u.Title} — {u.When}")" />
                                }
                            </MRowList>
                        }
                    </div>
                </MCard>
            </section>
        </div>

        @* ── ROW 2 — מצב הפרויקטים, full width ────────────────────────
             THE CENSUS, NOT A SECOND ATTENTION LIST — unchanged in what it
             answers, its three HealthBuckets groups, their server-side
             counts and their two-team cap.

             WHAT CHANGED IS THE COLOUR. The three counts were drawn rose /
             blue / teal, which made the hue a second copy of the label
             beside it and spent three of the product's four semantic roles
             on "which column am I in". They read dark now, with one
             exception: בסיכון keeps rose, because a project at risk is the
             one group on this card that names a problem. The dots follow the
             same three rungs the rest of the lecturer experience uses —
             rose, restrained brand, neutral. *@
        <div class="ldh-row ldh-row-2">
            @* ldh-pane-solid: this surface is opaque white rather than the
               translucent section fill the two cards above use — see the
               rule's own note. It is the only card on the page short
               enough that the shared violet wash never reaches its fade
               point, so the wash tinted it end to end instead of warming
               its top. Border, shadow and radius are unchanged. *@
            <section class="ldh-pane ldh-pane-solid" aria-labelledby="ldh-pf-h">
                <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.None" Fill="true">
                    <div class="ldh-card ldh-card-pf">
                        <div class="ldh-card-head">
                            @* NO LINK ON THIS HEADING. Its full-list action is
                               anchored at the foot of the card instead — see
                               .ldh-pf-foot. One action, one route; the heading
                               row is left to name the section. *@
                            <MSectionHeading Class="ldh-head" Text="מצב הפרויקטים"
                                             LabelId="ldh-pf-h">
                                <Icon>
                                    <span class="ldh-ico">
                                        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="url(#ldhIconGradient)"
                                             stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                            <path d="M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"></path>
                                            <circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"></circle>
                                            <path d="M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"></path>
                                        </svg>
                                    </span>
                                </Icon>
                            </MSectionHeading>
                        </div>

                        @if (_data.Summary.TotalProjects == 0)
                        {
                            <MEmptyState Title="אין פרויקטים פעילים בשנה הנוכחית."
                                         Class="ldh-empty" />
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <div class="ldh-groups">
                                @foreach (var g in PortfolioGroups)
                                {
                                    <div class="@($"ldh-group ldh-tone-{g.Tone}")">
                                        <div class="ldh-group-head">
                                            <span class="ldh-group-count">@g.Count</span>
                                            <span class="ldh-group-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                                            <span class="ldh-group-label">@g.Label</span>
                                        </div>

                                        @if (g.Count == 0)
                                        {
                                            <p class="ldh-group-calm">אין</p>
                                        }
                                        else if (g.IsHealthy)
                                        {
                                            @* The healthy group is a COUNT, not a list.
                                               Naming four teams that need nothing is the
                                               long list this dashboard is meant to spare
                                               the reader; the number is the whole fact. *@
                                            <p class="ldh-group-calm">מתקדמים לפי התוכנית</p>
                                        }
                                        else
                                        {
                                            @* MRow, with the stage in the META slot rather
                                               than as a second line. That keeps the census
                                               row on ONE line — the shape this card was
                                               built around — while still being the product's
                                               row rather than a private one. *@
                                            <MRowList AriaLabel="@g.Label">
                                                @foreach (var t in g.Teams)
                                                {
                                                    <MRow Primary="@t.Name"
                                                          Meta="@t.Stage"
                                                          Tooltip="@($"{t.Name} — {t.Stage}")"
                                                          Class="ldh-pf-row" />
                                                }
                                            </MRowList>

                                            @* Never a silent cap: if the group is
                                               deeper than the rows shown, the row
                                               count says so and /projects has the rest. *@
                                            @if (g.Hidden > 0)
                                            {
                                                <a class="ldh-pf-more" href="/projects">
                                                    @(g.Hidden == 1 ? "צוות נוסף" : $"עוד {g.Hidden} צוותים")
                                                </a>
                                            }
                                        }
                                    </div>
                                }
                            </div>

                            @* ── The card's closing action ──────────────────
                                 Anchored at the foot rather than floating in
                                 the heading row, because this is the surface
                                 that ends the page and a bottom edge with
                                 nothing on it does not read as finished.

                                 Same treatment as המשימות שלי's own footer
                                 link: centred, muted at caption weight, a pill
                                 wash on hover and nothing at rest. It carries
                                 no chip, no count and no leading mark, so it
                                 cannot be mistaken for a fourth group. Same
                                 /projects the heading link pointed at. *@
                            <div class="ldh-pf-foot">
                                <a class="ldh-pf-all" href="/projects">לצפייה מלאה</a>
                            </div>
                        }
                    </div>
                </MCard>
            </section>
        </div>
    }

</div>

@* ── Attention popup ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Unchanged in structure, behaviour and destinations — the same overlay,
   the same backdrop-to-close, the same detail rows, note and CTA. Only its
   surface, radii, chips and dividers moved onto the finished design's
   values. *@
@if (_popup is not null)
{
    <div class="ldh-overlay" @onclick="ClosePopup" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="ldh-popup-shell" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="@_popup.Title">
        <div class="ldh-popup">

            <div class="ldh-popup-header">
                @TagChip(_popup.Tag, _popup.Tone)
                <button type="button" class="ldh-popup-close" @onclick="ClosePopup" aria-label="סגור">
                    <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                         stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                        <path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"></path>
                    </svg>
                </button>
            </div>

            <h3 class="ldh-popup-title">@_popup.Title</h3>
            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_popup.TeamName))
            {
                <p class="ldh-popup-team">@_popup.TeamName</p>
            }

            <div class="ldh-popup-rows">
                @foreach (var row in _popup.Rows)
                {
                    <div class="ldh-popup-row">
                        <span class="ldh-popup-row-label">@row.Label</span>
                        <span class="@($"ldh-popup-row-val ldh-ink-{row.Tone}")">@row.Value</span>
                    </div>
                }
            </div>

            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_popup.Note))
            {
                <div class="@($"ldh-popup-note ldh-tone-{_popup.Tone}")">
                    <span class="ldh-popup-note-label">@_popup.NoteLabel</span>
                    <p class="ldh-popup-note-text">@_popup.Note</p>
                </div>
            }

            <div class="ldh-popup-footer">
                <button type="button" class="ldh-popup-btn-close" @onclick="ClosePopup">סגור</button>
                @* .motiva-cta is the shared primary treatment — the same
                   gradient, radius and hover every finished primary action in
                   the product wears. The page keeps only its geometry. *@
                <a class="ldh-popup-cta motiva-cta" href="@_popup.Href">@_popup.CtaLabel</a>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
}

@code {
    // ── The shared visual vocabulary ──────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // Every one of these hands a decision to a component or to the token
    // scope instead of making it here. Between them they are the whole of
    // what this page used to say in private CSS classes.

    /// <summary>The section count, for MSectionHeading — which renders it as
    /// `.motiva-count`, the product-wide bubble. A zero renders nothing at
    /// all, so a queue that has emptied stops advertising itself. Identical
    /// to המשימות שלי's own helper.</summary>
    private static string? CountLabel(int count) => count == 0 ? null : count.ToString();

    /// <summary>
    /// A kind tag, as MStatusBadge — the same chip המשימות שלי draws.
    ///
    /// <para><b>The four tones collapse onto two.</b> They were alert (rose),
    /// request (violet), wait (blue) and ok (teal): four hues telling you
    /// which of four categories a row belonged to, which the row's own words
    /// already say. Colour answers a different question now — is this a
    /// problem — so the two kinds that name one take rose, and the kind that
    /// names ordinary work in flight takes the restrained brand chip.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>"הגשות חסרות" is rose deliberately: Summary.SubmissionsMissing
    /// counts required submissions PAST DUE with nothing attached, so it is a
    /// genuine exception and not merely a queue. "החלטה נדרשת" is not — a
    /// request waiting for a decision has no deadline anywhere in this
    /// product's data, and rose there would assert a fact nothing holds.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private static RenderFragment TagChip(string label, string tone) => @<MStatusBadge
        Size="MStatusBadge.BadgeSize.Small"
        Variant="@TagVariant(tone)"
        Text="@label" />;

    private static MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant TagVariant(string tone) => tone switch
    {
        "alert" => MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant.Rose,       // פרויקט בסיכון
        "wait"  => MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant.Rose,       // הגשות חסרות — past due
        _       => MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant.Attention,  // החלטה נדרשת
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// לוח זמנים's timing chip — the milestone's position in time, in the
    /// same three-rung ladder המשימות שלי's waiting-age chip uses, so a
    /// lecturer learns one escalation across the role.
    ///
    /// <para><c>past</c> rose · <c>today</c>/<c>soon</c> the restrained brand
    /// tint · everything else neutral. Rose reaches ONLY the timing chip: the
    /// milestone title and its project stay in ordinary ink however late the
    /// date is, because the row is not the problem — the date is.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>Nothing here decides WHEN a milestone is late. That is
    /// UpcomingItems' own four steps, unchanged, from the same
    /// CurrentMilestoneDueDate.</para></summary>
    private static RenderFragment WhenChip(string label, string whenClass) => @<MStatusBadge
        Size="MStatusBadge.BadgeSize.Small"
        Variant="@WhenVariant(whenClass)"
        Text="@label" />;

    private static MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant WhenVariant(string whenClass) => whenClass switch
    {
        "past"           => MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant.Rose,
        "today" or "soon"=> MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant.Attention,
        _                => MStatusBadge.BadgeVariant.Neutral,
    };

    /// <summary>Ink for a date in MRow's meta slot. Rose when the date has
    /// genuinely passed and muted for every other step.
    ///
    /// <para>"today" and "soon" were blue and violet — two more category
    /// colours on two ordinary states of a schedule that is working. The
    /// relative wording ("היום", "עוד 3 ימים") is what tells them apart, and
    /// it is on the same line.</para></summary>
    private static MRow.RowMetaTone DueMetaTone(string whenClass) =>
        whenClass == "past" ? MRow.RowMetaTone.Rose : MRow.RowMetaTone.Default;

    /// <summary>בקרוב's secondary line: the project, and the date itself when
    /// the meta slot is showing a relative phrase rather than the date. The
    /// two never say the same thing.</summary>
    private static string UpcomingContext(UpcomingItem u)
    {
        var date = u.Date.ToString("d/M", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);
        // At the "default" step the meta slot already IS the date.
        if (u.WhenClass == "default") return u.Context;
        return string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(u.Context) ? date : $"{u.Context} · {date}";
    }

    [CascadingParameter] private User? _user { get; set; }

    private DashboardOverviewDto? _data;
    private bool _loading   = true;
    private bool _loadError;

    private AttentionItem? _popup;

    // ── Time / greeting ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private string _greeting
    {
        get
        {
            var name = _user?.FirstName?.Trim();
            var hour = DateTime.Now.Hour;
            var part = hour < 12 ? "בוקר טוב"
                     : hour < 17 ? "צהריים טובים"
                     : hour < 21 ? "ערב טוב"
                     :             "לילה טוב";
            return string.IsNullOrEmpty(name) ? part : $"{part}, {name}";
        }
    }

    // ── Data loading ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        var result = await DashboardService.GetAsync("lecturer");
        _loadError = result is null;
        _data      = result;
        _loading   = false;
    }

    // ── Popup ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private void OpenPopup(AttentionItem item) => _popup = item;
    private void ClosePopup() => _popup = null;

    // ── Data models ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// One attention row.
    ///
    /// <para><paramref name="Tone"/> is one of the finished design's four
    /// semantic roles — alert · request · wait · ok — as a CSS modifier
    /// rather than a hex triple. Every colour this page used to carry as
    /// three inline literals per item (bar, chip background, chip ink) is one
    /// class now, resolved from the tokens in the stylesheet, so a hue
    /// changes in one place and cannot drift between the row, the chip and
    /// the popup that opens from it.</para>
    ///
    /// <para><paramref name="Urgency"/> is the BAR's two-hue split, which is
    /// a different question from the kind: "is something wrong" rather than
    /// "which list is this". See the note at the row's markup.</para></summary>
    private sealed record AttentionItem(
        string Tag, string Tone, string Urgency,
        string Title, string TeamName, string Fact, string? Due, string DueClass, string Href,
        IReadOnlyList<PopupRow> Rows, string? Note, string NoteLabel, string CtaLabel);

    private sealed record PopupRow(string Label, string Value, string Tone);

    private sealed record UpcomingItem(
        DateTime Date, string When, string WhenClass, string Title, string Context, int ProjectId);

    /// <summary>One health bucket of the portfolio: the server's own count,
    /// its label, its tone, and the teams inside it.</summary>
    private sealed record PortfolioGroup(
        string Label, string Tone, int Count, bool IsHealthy,
        IReadOnlyList<PortfolioTeam> Teams, int Hidden);

    /// <summary>A team in the census. Two facts and no more: who it is, and
    /// where it has got to. Deliberately NOT what is waiting on the lecturer —
    /// that is the queue's job, and stating it here as well is what made the
    /// old lower list a second copy of the card above.</summary>
    private sealed record PortfolioTeam(string Name, string Stage, int ProjectId);

    // ── Derived: attention items ──────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // UNCHANGED: same three sources, same order, same filters, same caps.

    private IReadOnlyList<AttentionItem> AttentionItems
    {
        get
        {
            if (_data is null) return Array.Empty<AttentionItem>();

            var items = new List<AttentionItem>();

            // At-risk projects — highest urgency
            foreach (var p in _data.Projects
                .Where(p => p.HealthBucket == HealthBuckets.AtRisk)
                .OrderBy(p => p.HealthScore)
                .Take(3))
            {
                items.Add(BuildItem(p,
                    tag: "פרויקט בסיכון",
                    tone: "alert", urgency: "alert",
                    // The score IS why the server put this project in the
                    // AtRisk bucket, and it is the same number the dialog's
                    // note already prints. One fact, not a run of counters.
                    fact: $"ציון בריאות {p.HealthScore}/100",
                    href: $"/projects/{p.ProjectId}/overview",
                    ctaLabel: "לפרויקט"));
            }

            // Open requests (lecturer decision needed)
            foreach (var p in _data.Projects
                .Where(p => p.OpenRequestCount > 0 && p.HealthBucket != HealthBuckets.AtRisk)
                .OrderByDescending(p => p.OpenRequestCount)
                .Take(3))
            {
                items.Add(BuildItem(p,
                    tag: "החלטה נדרשת",
                    tone: "request", urgency: "wait",
                    fact: p.OpenRequestCount == 1
                            ? "בקשה אחת ממתינה להחלטתך"
                            : $"{p.OpenRequestCount} בקשות ממתינות להחלטתך",
                    href: "/management/requests",
                    ctaLabel: "לבקשות"));
            }

            // Missing submissions (past due with nothing attached, no open
            // request, not at-risk). "הגשות חסרות" — the name the query's own
            // predicate earns, and the name BuildDesc below already used.
            foreach (var p in _data.Projects
                .Where(p => p.MissingSubmissionCount > 0 && p.OpenRequestCount == 0 && p.HealthBucket != HealthBuckets.AtRisk)
                .OrderByDescending(p => p.MissingSubmissionCount)
                .Take(2))
            {
                items.Add(BuildItem(p,
                    tag: "הגשות חסרות",
                    tone: "wait", urgency: "wait",
                    fact: p.MissingSubmissionCount == 1
                            ? "הגשה אחת חסרה"
                            : $"{p.MissingSubmissionCount} הגשות חסרות",
                    href: "/lecturer/submissions",
                    ctaLabel: "לבדיקה"));
            }

            return items.Take(6).ToList();
        }
    }

    private static AttentionItem BuildItem(
        DashboardProjectRowDto p,
        string tag, string tone, string urgency,
        string fact, string href, string ctaLabel)
    {
        var rows = new List<PopupRow>();
        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.MentorNames))
            rows.Add(new PopupRow("מנחה", p.MentorNames, "neutral"));
        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.CurrentMilestoneTitle))
            rows.Add(new PopupRow("אבן דרך", p.CurrentMilestoneTitle, "neutral"));
        if (p.CurrentMilestoneDueDate.HasValue)
            rows.Add(new PopupRow("תאריך יעד",
                p.CurrentMilestoneDueDate.Value.ToString("d/M/yyyy"),
                p.CurrentMilestoneDueDate.Value < DateTime.Today ? "alert" : "neutral"));
        if (p.OverdueTaskCount > 0)
            rows.Add(new PopupRow("משימות באיחור", p.OverdueTaskCount.ToString(), "alert"));
        if (p.MissingSubmissionCount > 0)
            rows.Add(new PopupRow("הגשות חסרות", p.MissingSubmissionCount.ToString(), "wait"));
        if (p.OpenRequestCount > 0)
            rows.Add(new PopupRow("בקשות פתוחות", p.OpenRequestCount.ToString(), "request"));

        string? note = null;
        string noteLabel = "הערה";
        if (p.HealthBucket == HealthBuckets.AtRisk)
        {
            note = $"ציון בריאות: {p.HealthScore:F0}/100 — הפרויקט דורש התערבות מיידית.";
            noteLabel = "מצב הפרויקט";
        }
        else if (p.OpenRequestCount > 0)
        {
            note = $"{p.OpenRequestCount} בקשות ממתינות לאישורך.";
            noteLabel = "נדרשת פעולה";
        }

        var (due, dueClass) = DueChip(p.CurrentMilestoneDueDate);

        return new AttentionItem(
            Tag: tag, Tone: tone, Urgency: urgency,
            Title: p.ProjectTitle,
            TeamName: p.TeamName ?? "",
            Fact: fact,
            Due: due, DueClass: dueClass,
            Href: href,
            Rows: rows,
            Note: note,
            NoteLabel: noteLabel,
            CtaLabel: ctaLabel);
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The project's deadline as a short chip, or null when it has no current
    /// milestone. Same four urgency steps as בקרוב, from the same
    /// CurrentMilestoneDueDate, so the two cards cannot colour one date two
    /// ways.
    ///
    /// <para><b>A DATE, NEVER AN AGE.</b> DashboardOverviewDto carries no
    /// timestamp for a request or a submission — only the project's milestone
    /// due date — so a bare relative phrase on a request row would be read as
    /// "this has waited N days", which nothing here can support. The chip is
    /// prefixed "יעד" and shows the date, and the tone is the only thing that
    /// says how urgent it is.</para></summary>
    private static (string? Text, string Class) DueChip(DateTime? due)
    {
        if (due is null) return (null, "default");

        int days = (due.Value.Date - DateTime.Today).Days;
        string cls = days <  0 ? "past"
                   : days == 0 ? "today"
                   : days <= 7 ? "soon"
                   :             "default";

        return ($"יעד {due.Value:d/M}", cls);
    }

    // ── Derived: the portfolio census ────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // NOTHING HERE IS COMPUTED. HealthBucket is assigned by
    // LecturerDashboardController from its own health formula and arrives on
    // every row; Charts.Health* are that same assignment counted, server-side,
    // over the same scope. This code groups and labels — it does not decide
    // what is healthy.

    /// <summary>How many teams each exception group names before deferring to
    /// /projects.
    ///
    /// <para>Two, and the number was chosen by measuring rather than by taste.
    /// The group is a POINTER at the teams worth opening, not the list of them
    /// — /projects is the list, and <c>Hidden</c> always says how many are not
    /// shown. At three, a full page (six attention rows, five dated entries,
    /// three teams in each of two groups) needed 834px and did not fit a
    /// 1440×900 laptop's ~798px of document height; the only ways to buy that
    /// back were squeezing every row on the page or naming one fewer team per
    /// group. Naming one fewer costs a pointer that is one click away
    /// anyway.</para></summary>
    private const int GroupRows = 2;

    /// <summary>
    /// The three buckets, worst-first.
    ///
    /// <para><b>The labels are this page's, and one of them differs from
    /// <see cref="HealthBuckets.Label"/> on purpose.</b> That helper calls the
    /// middle bucket "דורש תשומת לב", which on THIS screen is a third thing
    /// called תשומת לב — beside a card titled דורש את תשומת לבך and a chip row
    /// that used the phrase too. It reads as "these are the items in that
    /// card", which is exactly what the census is not. "דורש מעקב" says the
    /// same thing about the same bucket and cannot be confused with the queue.
    /// The shared helper is untouched and still correct everywhere else.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>Counts come from Charts, never from counting Teams: Teams is
    /// capped at <see cref="GroupRows"/> and the count must be the whole
    /// bucket.</para></summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<PortfolioGroup> PortfolioGroups
    {
        get
        {
            if (_data is null) return Array.Empty<PortfolioGroup>();

            return new[]
            {
                BuildGroup("בסיכון",    "alert", _data.Charts.HealthAtRisk,    HealthBuckets.AtRisk),
                BuildGroup("דורש מעקב", "wait",  _data.Charts.HealthAttention, HealthBuckets.Attention),
                BuildGroup("תקין",      "ok",    _data.Charts.HealthHealthy,   HealthBuckets.Healthy),
            };
        }
    }

    private PortfolioGroup BuildGroup(string label, string tone, int count, string bucket)
    {
        bool healthy = bucket == HealthBuckets.Healthy;

        // The healthy group never lists members — see the note at its markup.
        var members = healthy || _data is null
            ? new List<DashboardProjectRowDto>()
            : _data.Projects
                   .Where(p => p.HealthBucket == bucket)
                   .OrderBy(p => p.HealthScore)   // worst first, as everywhere else on this page
                   .ToList();

        var shown = members.Take(GroupRows)
                           .Select(p => new PortfolioTeam(
                               Name:      string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.TeamName) ? p.ProjectTitle : p.TeamName!,
                               Stage:     string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.CurrentMilestoneTitle)
                                              ? "טרם החל" : p.CurrentMilestoneTitle!,
                               ProjectId: p.ProjectId))
                           .ToList();

        return new PortfolioGroup(
            Label:     label,
            Tone:      tone,
            Count:     count,
            IsHealthy: healthy,
            Teams:     shown,
            Hidden:    Math.Max(0, members.Count - shown.Count));
    }

    /// <summary>The split bar's accessible name. The bar is a width; this is
    /// the same information as text, so the shape is never the only carrier.</summary>
    private string SplitLabel =>
        _data is null
            ? ""
            : $"{_data.Summary.TotalProjects} פרויקטים: " + string.Join(", ",
                  PortfolioGroups.Where(g => g.Count > 0).Select(g => $"{g.Count} {g.Label}"));

    // ── Derived: upcoming deadlines ───────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // UNCHANGED selection: the same projects, the same order, five deep, the
    // same relative phrasing. What moved is where each part is drawn — the
    // date onto a tile, the relative words and the project onto a meta line.

    private IEnumerable<UpcomingItem> UpcomingItems
    {
        get
        {
            if (_data is null) return Enumerable.Empty<UpcomingItem>();

            return _data.Projects
                .Where(p => p.CurrentMilestoneDueDate.HasValue)
                .OrderBy(p => p.CurrentMilestoneDueDate)
                .Take(5)
                .Select(p =>
                {
                    var d = p.CurrentMilestoneDueDate!.Value;
                    int days = (d.Date - DateTime.Today).Days;
                    string when;
                    string cls;

                    // Order matters: `days < 0` is tested BEFORE the `<= 7`
                    // band, which the previous chain reached only after
                    // `days <= 7` had already claimed every negative value —
                    // so an overdue milestone read "עוד -4 ימים" in the
                    // soon-violet instead of "לפני 4 ימים" in rose.
                    if (days < 0)        { when = $"לפני {-days} ימים"; cls = "past"; }
                    else if (days == 0)  { when = "היום";              cls = "today"; }
                    else if (days == 1)  { when = "מחר";               cls = "soon"; }
                    else if (days <= 7)  { when = $"עוד {days} ימים";   cls = "soon"; }
                    else                 { when = d.ToString("d/M", System.Globalization.CultureInfo.InvariantCulture); cls = "default"; }

                    // The milestone titles the row; the project is its
                    // context. Where a project has no current milestone
                    // title, the project takes the title line and the
                    // context is left empty rather than repeated.
                    bool hasMs = !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.CurrentMilestoneTitle);

                    return new UpcomingItem(
                        Date:      d,
                        When:      when,
                        WhenClass: cls,
                        Title:     hasMs ? p.CurrentMilestoneTitle! : p.ProjectTitle,
                        Context:   hasMs ? p.ProjectTitle : "",
                        ProjectId: p.ProjectId);
                });
        }
    }
}
